<h3 class="text-base font-bold text-gray-800 mb-2">Terms and Condition</h3>
<p>By proceeding, you agree to participate in Compass, a peer-support platform designed to provide emotional support through trained psychology student helpers.</p>
<p>Please read the following carefully:</p>
<ul class="space-y-2">
<li>This service is NOT a form of professional counseling, psychotherapy, diagnosis, or treatment.</li>
<li>The listener is a trained psychology student helpers providing peer support and is not a licensed psychologist or mental health professional.</li>
<li>The purpose of this platform is to provide emotional support through listening, empathy, and supportive conversation.</li>
<li>Your participation in this service is voluntary, and you may end the session or discontinue using the platform at any time without penalty.</li>
<li>The information you provide will be treated with confidentiality. However, measures are implemented to protect your privacy.</li>
<li>To support service quality and helper development, anonymous session summaries, risk tags, satisfaction ratings, and related records may be reviewed by authorized advisers for supervision and performance evaluation purposes. Raw session transcripts or recordings shall only be accessed when necessary for abuse investigations, helper misconduct reviews, quality assurance, or when your consent has been obtained.</li>
<li>If your situation appears to require professional intervention, you may be offered referral options to a licensed mental health professional. Referral services will only proceed upon your consent, and you may be asked to voluntarily provide contact information for scheduling purposes.</li>
<li>In situations involving an imminent risk of serious self-harm or harm to others, Project Dial-A-Friend may encourage you to disclose the information necessary to facilitate emergency assistance in accordance with ethical obligations and the duty to protect principle.</li>
<li>This service is available for live peer-support sessions only between 6:00 PM and 11:00 PM (PHT) and is dependent on the availability of helper listeners. Sessions outside these hours may not receive immediate responses.</li>
<li>Voice call sessions are subject to a maximum duration of one (1) hour and thirty (30) minutes to ensure equitable access to support services and helper well-being.</li>
<li>Use of this platform is subject to respectful and appropriate behavior. Abusive, threatening, harassing, or malicious use of the service may result in termination of the session and restriction from future access.</li>
<li>Data collected through this platform shall be processed in accordance with applicable privacy laws, including the Data Privacy Act of 2012 (Republic Act No. 10173), and shall only be used for purposes related to service delivery, supervision, referral coordination, system improvement, and approved research activities.</li>
<li>If you are in immediate danger or experiencing severe distress, please use the Emergency Button or contact local crisis hotlines immediately.</li>
</ul>